hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17359","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Harb, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Malik Abi Jafar, from Abi Nadrah, from Sad ibn al-Atwal, he said: My brother died and left three hundred dinars and left small children, so I wanted to spend upon them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Your brother is detained by his debt, so go and pay on his behalf. He said: So I went and paid on his behalf, then I came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have paid on his behalf, and none remains except a woman claiming two dinars, and she has no proof. He said: Give her, for she is truthful."
"20336","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik Abu Jafar informed us from Abu Nadrah from Sad ibn al-Atwal, that his brother died leaving three hundred dirhams and leaving dependents. I wanted to spend it upon his dependents, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother is confined by his debt, so settle it for him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have paid for him except two dinars claimed by a woman and she has no proof. He said: Give them to her, for she is truthful."
"20337","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
